         "id": "introduction",
         "target": "",
         "page": "",
         "value_type": "",
         "html_value": [
            {
               "text": "<p><hr /></p><p><h3>Physics and the Universe</h3>The science of Physics goes beyond the limits of planet Earth and, through its studies, provides us with essential information about our universe.</p><p>Like any science, Physics is also directly connected to the language of mathematics. For this reason, we begin this section with Chapter 6 of the <i>First Steps</i> part, which is dedicated to the study of mathematics in connection with other sciences. Thus, we recommend reading the first five chapters of that section before continuing (<htcite0>).</p><p>Although in school we are introduced to subjects called Science or Physics before entering university, teaching often limits itself to presenting only the initial stages of this field. These stages could be referred to as proto-Physics or pre-Physics, as proposed by Dr. Francisco González A. Redondo (<htcite1>; <htcite2>; <htcite3>; <htcite4>).</p></p>In the texts of this section, we present the concepts of pre-Physics and proto-Physics, gradually connecting them to Physics through mathematics.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
